      4 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اظلف</span></b> , said of a man, (IAar, T, O,) or of a
company of men, (M,) <i>He,</i> or <i>they, became,</i> or
<i>came to be,</i> (IAar, T, M, O, K,) <i>in,</i> or <i>upon, a
hard place,</i> (IAar, T, O,) or <i>in,</i> or <i>upon, what
is termed</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أُظْلُوفَة</span> (M, K) and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ظَلَف</span>. (M.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2- 
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اظلفهُ</span>: see 1, in two places.

